---
import Layout from '../../layouts.astro';
import { manifest } from '../../lib/spec';
---
<Layout title="MCP"><h1>MCP</h1><p>The production server targets MCP <strong>2026-07-28</strong> using the official TypeScript SDK v2 and stateless <code>createMcpHandler</code>.</p><h2>Public resources</h2><pre>{`style://manifest\nstyle://principles\nstyle://tokens\nstyle://components\nstyle://components/button\nstyle://patterns\nstyle://accessibility\nstyle://anti-patterns\nstyle://decisions\nstyle://version`}</pre><h2>Read tools</h2><pre>{`get_style_manifest\nget_design_tokens\nget_component_rules\nsearch_style_spec\nexplain_style_decision\nvalidate_tokens\ncheck_style_compliance\ncompare_spec_versions`}</pre><h2>One-call constitution generation</h2><p>When <code>MCP_ENABLE_WRITES=true</code> and <code>MCP_ENABLE_AI_ORCHESTRATION=true</code>, an authenticated client can call <code>generate_style_constitution_candidate</code> with a product brief. Astra and Fable receive the same frozen context independently, cross-review, revise for a bounded number of rounds, and only produce a candidate when conflicts are gone and deterministic validation passes.</p><p>The generated candidate is still not a release. Astra/Fable exact-hash approvals remain required. The optional <code>publish_release</code> tool is separately disabled by default and, when enabled, requires a distinct human-held approval token in addition to admin authorization.</p><h2>Version</h2><p>{manifest.version}</p></Layout>
